## Aug 12 batch (GFlowNet 2608.10171 · REDAgentBench 2608.10669 · Cross-lingual 2608.11146)

- **K270 GFlowNet attacks (lab)** — GFlowNet-trained attacker-victim-evaluator attack generation for LLMs is a **scoped, authorized-lab eval primitive** (owned victims / written scope); report **dual metrics** (overall ASR vs phase/attack-success + diversity/similarity) and the evaluator classifier used — the evaluator choice flips which attacker "wins". REFERENCE only (no public code); do not run against LIVE third-party targets.
- **K271 REDAgentBench (lab + audit)** — executable agent red-teaming: **do not collapse exposure / execution / observation / adjudication into one ASR**; report ASR as `(harness, judging configuration, evaluation cue, judge backbone)` and prefer state-grounded verification (service receipts / final-state diffs) over trajectory self-report. Use the Recognition–Execution Gap and the action-time policy reminder as diagnostic/repair probes. REFERENCE (benchmark not yet released).
- **K272 Cross-lingual safety (lab)** — English-only safety eval ≠ low-resource-language safety: for any deployment serving non-English users, run **lab eval in the target languages with culturally localized prompts** (not literal translations); expect refusal-direction retention <10% in LRLs (7B–8B open models). Authorized lab only; no LIVE target-language probing. REFERENCE (LoDNA not yet public).

